{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfsuenuuQ8K6GRZstDghg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"These are exactly the kind of details that make the difference between a portfolio that's accurate and one that's just handsome. Updating the plan now, and I'll flag what still needs your call.\n\n**Revisions to the plan:**\n\n- **Calder Court copy** changes from implying authorship to the true scope: concept by the partner, Marta as project architect from technical design through handover — the detailing, the wall build-up, the site. The section will say that plainly, not \"designed by.\"\n- **The 68% figure** gets a label, not a headline claim: \"modelled — 68% less heating demand; in-use monitoring begins winter 2026.\" No bar chart drawn to look like a measured result.\n- **Titles**: Associate throughout, nowhere \"Architect\" as a current role (the plan already did this, now confirmed deliberate given the CV is outdated).\n- **Rights, as a pre-build gate, not an afterthought**: Tom Reid's photos (Calder Court + Kirk Street) need sign-off from him and the practice, with credit to him wherever used. The practice's drawings need the practice's permission even though she drew the detail herself. Nothing from those two projects gets built into the live site until that's cleared — I'd suggest we build those sections with placeholder space first and drop in real material once you've asked.\n- **Cabin at Kashuby** needs no permission — it's the one section we can build fully and immediately, text and image treatment both. That strengthens the case for it being the most developed, textured part of the site, as planned.\n- **School boards** get credited as a team of four, with her specific contribution named: structure and sections. Not presented as solo work.\n\n**New material this changes the plan:**\n\n- **Who it's for** reframes the contact/footer entirely. This isn't a general \"get in touch\" — it's aimed at two people: someone with an old house or a small plot, and a school that needs a guest critic. I'd write the close to speak to both by name, plainly, rather than a generic form. One open question for you: you're currently an Associate at Field & Rowe — how direct do you want the site to be about wanting your own practice in two years? I can write this as a soft undertone (the work itself implies it) or state it outright. Your call, since it touches your current employer.\n- **How you work** — the RIBA stages 0–7, the drawing set order (location, plans, sections, elevations, details, schedules), the snag list — is good material for exactly the audience you named. Someone with an old house doesn't know what an architect does month to month; this demystifies it and builds trust before they ever email you. I'd add it as a short section, either folded into the Practice timeline or standing alone just before Contact. Leaning toward standalone, since it's written for the client, not for other architects reading your CV.\n- **Influences** (your father's workshop, the Swiss timber joints book since you were nineteen) — this goes into the Cabin section as a quiet caption-level detail, not a callout. It's the kind of thing that earns trust by being understated rather than announced.\n\n**Open questions before I move forward:**\n\n1. Build Calder Court/Kirk Street now with placeholder photo space, or hold those sections until permissions are back?\n2. How explicit about the future-practice ambition in the contact copy?\n3. \"How I work\" as its own section, or merged into the timeline?\n\nOnce you've weighed in on those, I'll treat the plan as settled and move to building."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5648,"cache_read_input_tokens":18261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5648},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"134855d6-b9ca-4cc7-8738-2c388ac7d382","uuid":"3ad3d7ac-4ab7-49ac-b2f7-ca67d89bbf2d","timestamp":"2026-10-10T04:16:44.902Z","request_id":"req_011Cfsuenh1CG5KT9V6KgdJz"}
